The food looks like a meatloaf slice or a similar loaf-shaped item, glazed on top. The plate looks like a dinner plate of about 26 cm, and the food is about 12 cm long and 7 cm wide. Its height is about 3-4 cm, so the volume is roughly 12 × 7 × 3.5 ≈ 290 cm³. Allowing for the tapered shape, I'd put it at about 220 cm³. At a density of about 1 g/cm³, that comes to roughly 200 g.

If it is meatloaf, at about 1.9 kcal/g, 200 g would be about 380 kcal. The glaze may add a little more. The brown, dense texture could also mean a brownie-like cake or a dense loaf, but the estimate would be similar either way.

